./ ALIAS NAME=AD                                                                
)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The ADDSD command defines a profile in the DATASET class.                     
  It writes one line in the PROFILES member of SYS1.SECURE.CNTL.                
                                                                                
  ADDSD updates the control data sets on disk only.  Reload the in              
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFPROF' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFPROF procedure in batch, or the profile is not in             
  effect.                                                                       
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group.  ADDSD is an ordinary             
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
                                                                                
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  ADDSD 'data set profile' UACC(NONE/READ/UPDATE/ALTER)                         
                                                                                
  ALIAS - AD                                                                    
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - 'data set profile'                                                 
  DEFAULT  - UACC(NONE)                                                         
                                                                                
  EXAMPLE  - ADDSD SYS1.* UACC(READ)                                            
                                                                                
  The operands can be shortened to the shortest unique abbreviation.            
  So, AD SYS1.* U(READ) is also valid.                                          
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The DATASET profile is created.                                        
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))'data set profile' - the profile in the DATASET class. The                    
  length can be up to 44 bytes. Generic profiles can be created.                
))UACC - Specify the universal access of the profile.                           
  possible values are: NONE (no access), READ, UPDATE and                       
  ALTER (delete and create).                                                    
                                                                                
